gram\nHemoglobinopathies Topics-in-Focus program\nCongress\nHemaSphere\nAbout EHA\nSearch\nJoin EHA\nLogin\nHome\nResearch & Innovation\nSpecialized Working Groups\nSWG Grants\nSWG Grant-funded projects, 2025\nLeft Sidebar\n2 min read · May 1, 2025\nMay 1, 2025\nShare\nSWG Grants\nSWG Grant-funded projects, 2026\nSWG Grant-funded projects, 2025\nBiology of Hodgkin lymphoma in older patients project\nGaucher disease non-interventional clinical audit study\nSecondary leukemogenesis in the context of T-cell based immunotherapies project\nEpidemiology of infection in AML: A European Hematology Association survey (EPIAMLINF)\nCRYSTAL-Immune pump-priming project\nBiology of Hodgkin lymphoma in older patients project update, December 2025\nCRYSTAL-Immune pump-priming project update, December 2025\nEpidemiology of Infection in Acute Myeloid Leukaemia (EPIAMLINF) project update, March 2026\nGaucher disease non-interventional clinical audit study project update, February 2026\nSWG Grant-funded projects, 2024\nSWG Grant-funded projects, 2023\nSWG Grant-funded projects, 2025\nIn November and December 2024, SWGs were invited to develop project ideas and apply for a 2025 SWG Grant.\nFor the 2025 call, EHA offered five grants, each worth €30,000. This was an increase on the previous funding level, which was three grants of €20,000 each. The EHA Board made this change in recognition of the increased interest in the grant from SWG members.\nApplications\nWe received 15 different applications from nine SWGs. This was four more applications than we received in 2023 and six more than in 2022.\nThese applications came from the:\nSWG on Immune Therapies for Hematologic Disorders (2 applications)\nSWG on Myelodysplastic Syndromes (MDS) (1 application)\nSWG on Infections in Hematology (1 application)\nSWG on Granulocytes and Constitutional Marrow Failure Disorders (2 applications)\nEHA Lymphoma Group (2 applications)\nSWG on Red Cells and Iron (2 applications)\nSWG on Pediatric Hematology (2 applications)\nSWG on Genetic predisposition to blood cancers (rare diseases) (1 application)\nSWG on Aging in Hematology (2 applications)\nWinners\nAll applications were reviewed against our selection criteria by SWG Committee members. These criteria are explained on the main SWG Grants page.\nAfter careful consideration and fruitful discussion, the SWG Committee chose the following winners:\nEpidemiology of infection in AML: A European Hematology Association survey (EPIAMLINF) (SWG on Infections in Hematology)\nGaucher disease (GD) non-interventional clinical audit study (SWG on Granulocytes and Constitutional Marrow Failure Disorders)\nUnraveling the biological landscape of Hodgkin lymphoma in older patients (joint application from SWG on Aging in Hematology and EHA Lymphoma group)\nSecondary leukemogenesis in the context of T-cell based immunotherapies (SWG on Immune Therapies for Hematologic Disorders)\nCRYSTAL-Immune pump-priming (SWG on Pediatric Hematology)\nShare\nSWG Grants\nSWG Grant-funded projects, 2026\nSWG Grant-funded projects, 2025\nBiology of Hodgkin lymphoma in older patients project\nGaucher disease non-interventional clinical audit study\nSecondary leukemogenesis in the context of T-cell based immunotherapies project\nEpidemiology of infection in AML: A European Hematology Association survey (EPIAMLINF)\nCRYSTAL-Immune pump-priming project\nBiology of Hodgkin lymphoma in older patients project update, December 2025\nCRYSTAL-Immune pump-priming project update, December 2025\nEpidemiology of Infection in Acute Myeloid Leukaemia (EPIAMLINF) project update, March 2026\nGaucher disease non-interventional clinical audit study project update, February 2026\nSWG Grant-funded projects, 2024\nSWG Grant-funded projects, 2023\nJoin EHA\nFull membership\nJunior membership\n60-day trial\nGet involved\nCareer development\nScientific meetings\nAbout us\nMission and vision\nJobs\nSponsor EHA\nContact us\nFollow us\nPrivacy statement\nTerms and conditions\nSub